{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed. The second publish included similarity scores as Python floats, which DynamoDB rejects. The first publish had no related stories, so it avoided the issue.\n\n- `src/app.py` now converts scores to `Decimal` before storage.\n- `tests/test_publish.py` adds a two-publish regression test covering the 500 response and stored score type.\n- `ANSWER.md` documents the cause and fix.\n- Verification: `python3 -m unittest discover tests` — **2 tests passed**."}
